 Medicine Storage Guardian: An IoT-Based Intelligent Medicine Storage System

Project ID:PRJ_282
Author: Benitha Christinal J  
Affiliation: School of Computer Science and Engineering, Presidency University Bangalore  



 Project Overview
A low-cost, continuous IoT monitoring solution designed to track environmental conditions (temperature and humidity) inside medicine storage units to ensure medication stability and prevent breakdown.

Hardware & Tools
Microcontroller:ESP32 / ESP8266
Sensors: DHT22 / DHT11 (Temperature & Humidity)
Output / Display: OLED Display, Buzzer / LED
IoT Protocols & Cloud: InfluxDB, Cloud/Server Layer, Email/SMS Alerts

System Architecture
1. Device Layer:Captures real-time sensor readings.
2. Gateway & Network Layer: Edge data processing & time-series logging.
3. Rules Engine:Checks upper/lower threshold boundaries.
4. Notification Layer:Triggers local audible/visual alarms and digital alerts.
